# Stable export baseline for libminitun-remote-protocol.so.1.
#
# One entry per public API symbol, written as a mangled-name prefix. The prefix
# pins the namespace, class, method name, and everything up to the first
# parameter, while deliberately leaving the trailing standard-library type
# mangling (libstdc++ vs libc++ spellings of std::string_view, std::variant,
# std::span, std::array) out of the comparison. Adding, removing, or re-signing
# a public method changes this list and fails sdk.remote-protocol-abi.
#
# The library is a C++20 ABI surface: consumers must build with a compatible
# standard library. See docs/sdk.md.

